# Reconsider the approach

Stop implementing when the approach creates compensating problems, a load-bearing assumption fails, a consequential design fork appears, or actual scope invalidates the plan.

Preserve current work and the pinned baseline; do not reset or discard evidence. Record the failed assumption, observed evidence, alternatives, and scope impact in the card. Use a [spike](./spike.md) only for a concrete executable uncertainty.

Revise the approach within the card's scope. Honor plan approval gates before resuming; request user direction when scope or a consequential choice remains unresolved. Once settled, [reroute the next unit](./implementation.md).
